WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.200
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.200
at-home retreat.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.920
And I'd like to thank Stanley again for translating,

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.080
thanks for staying in America and translating.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.700
We're on Session 21.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.260
It's called "Seeing that the Jail is a Jail."

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.960
And the picture is a jail.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.350
We actually used to have a very active program of teaching lam rim (LAM RIM) in the jails.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.626
And it helped the prisoners a lot,

00:00:51.626 --> 00:00:55.460
and the government thanked us because the prisoners gor less fights.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.940
The picture you see here is kind of perfect for a jail because

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.780
it's really depressing in a jail.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.380
So when we study the Wheel of Life in the monastery,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.180
we study it from a set of books called sur kol (ZUR BKOL).

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.799
And it's a tradition to take about five different subjects,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.060
and you squeeze special subjects out of bigger books,

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.960
like the way you would squeeze medicine out of an herb.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.080
And for our computer project, saving the ancient books,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.951
that was actually the first book we ever printed

00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:24.226
was called sur kol--the five books

00:02:24.226 --> 00:02:26.500
that are extracted from the big books.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.720
And you'll be interested to know

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.020
that the whole Wheel of Life teaching

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.220
as it is taught in the monastery

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.040
and we study it for about 2-3 months,

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.160
It all comes from one line from Maitreya.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.900
I should say one verse, not one line.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.020
And I think you've heard me say this line before:

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.857
de ne sengge nam gyingpay
ting-nge-dzin la nyom shuk ne
ten ching drel jung luk tun dang
luk mi tun la tokpay che

00:03:15.857 --> 00:03:20.019
(DE NAS SENG GE RNAM BSGYINGS PA'I,
,TING NGE 'DZIN LA SNYOMS ZHUGS NAS,
,RTEN CING 'BREL 'BYUNG LUGS MTHUN DANG, 
,LUGS MI MTHUN LA RTOG PAR BYED,)

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:23.409
It teaches both the Lion's Dance

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.970
and the Wheel of Life.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.668
And the part that I want to talk about today

00:03:31.668 --> 00:03:34.080
is the ending part.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.000
It says ten ching drel jung luk tun dang luk mi tun
(RTEN CING 'BREL 'BYUNG LUGS MTHUN DANG LUGS MI MTHUN)

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.580
luk tun dang luk mi tun
(LUGS MTHUN DANG LUGS MI MTHUN)--

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:51.100
luk tun (LUGS MTHUN) means one triggers two, two triggers three, three triggers four, etc.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.720
The wife in the kitchen says, "I didn't do anything--he yelled at me!"

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:00.940
So that's link number one.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.060
Then she yells back,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.550
That's luk tun means "normal order."

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.920
Then luk mi tun (LUGS MI MTHUN), which is sometimes called luk dok (LUGS LDOG)--

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.439
it means "to turn (the wheel) backwards,"

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.990
to shut down the wheel.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:34.020
So, you kind of think, "Oh, it must be since it says backwards,

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.659
it must go from twelve, to eleven, to ten.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.760
First I die,

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:49.830
then I get old, then I get born, then my karma gets fat,

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.610
then I arm the karma."

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.479
I mean you could have some strange ideas like that.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.279
But here in the lam rim, they describe what it really means to turn the wheel around.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.460
de dak luk dok tu gog nupay lam shik nyam su len na
(DE DAG LUGS LDOG TU 'GOG NUS PA'I LAM ZHIG NYAMS SU LEN NA)--

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.800
so we are following the Tibetan--

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.420
de dak luk dok tu gog nupay lam shik nyam su len na,

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.340
if you undertake a path

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.940
which will enable you

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.660
to stop the wheel of life by reversing it.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.400
So, what does it mean to reverse the wheel of life, to shut down the wheel of life?

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.080
marikpa gakpe duje gak
(MA RIG PA 'GAG PAS 'DU BYED 'GAGS)--

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.220
if you stop misunderstanding, then you stop making karma.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.240
Let's take it to the kitchen,

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.460
which is where you should take all your Dharma.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:08.470
If you can't take it to the kitchen, it's not Dharma.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:18.580
Okay, and what, if it is Dharma, then you should be able to take it to the kitchen. Something like that.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:28.420
There shouldn't be anything in the 300,000 books of Buddhism that we have that you cannot find in the kitchen.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:42.099
And if something good or bad is happening in the kitchen, it must be described in the ancient books.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.620
Because the ancient books were written for the kitchen.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.520
marikpa gakpe duje gak

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.860
means if she can stop having

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.600
misunderstanding about her husband,

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.360
if she doesn't say, "I don't know why he yelled at me,"

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.600
She says, "Ah, I know why he yelled at me!

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.880
I was yelling at my kids last week."

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.580
She just reversed the first link.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.080
She just blocked the first link.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.399
If you block that "I didn't do anything,"

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:45.020
then automatically, you will not reach the second link--

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.680
"I am not stupid; you are stupid!"

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:54.340
Okay good.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.520
So if you stop the first link, then the second link will never come.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.040
So that's how we stop the Wheel of Life.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.760
Don't forget Wheel of Life is a kind of a bad name, misnomer.

00:08:16.159 --> 00:08:18.218
It's not really the Wheel of Life.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:21.550
I mean, a Buddha also has life.

00:08:23.259 --> 00:08:26.799
It means the wheel of bad life and painful life.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.440
marikpa gakpe duje gakpa ne
(MA RIG PA 'GAG PAS 'DU BYED 'GAGS PA NAS)--

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.440
if you stop link number one, you stop link number two.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.080
Eventually, you'll stop everything up to getting old and dying.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.431
dukgnel tamche gakpar gyur ro
(SDUG BSNGAL THAMS CAD 'GAG PAR 'GYUR RO)--

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.840
all the pain in your life will be stopped.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:04.700
Also don't think Wheel of Life means if you get out of the Wheel of Life you have to die or disappear.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:14.319
In the Wheel of Life, for example, in the painting,

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.660
the Buddha is outside the wheel

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.289
and he's pointing to the moon,

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.860
which represents Nirvana.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.980
Ok, let's go back to the text.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:35.440
dor du na, tendrel yenlak chu nyi le dang nyonmong dukngel gyi tendrel sum dundu te
(MDOR BSDU NA, RTEN 'BREL YAN LAG BCU GNYIS LAS DANG NYON MONGS SDUG BSNGAL GYI RTEN 'BREL GSUM DU 'DU STE)

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.780
dor du na (MDOR BSDU NA) means "let's kind of summarize everything."

00:09:43.279 --> 00:09:45.279
You can take all twelve links,

00:09:48.829 --> 00:09:56.198
and just for summary, we can divide them differently than many ways we divided them before.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.780
We can divide them into number one: karma,

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:12.780
number two: negative thoughts,

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.740
and number three: pain.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.400
Okay, you can divide into those three.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.267
marikpa dang sepa lenpa sun nyonmong
(MA RIG PA DANG, SRED PA, LEN PA GSUM NYON MONGS)--

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:29.289
three of the links are negative emotions.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.660
That's misunderstanding your husband.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.600
And then sepa (SRED PA) we've been saying like negative coffee meditation.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:46.540
"Are you sorry that you yelled at your husband?" "No."

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:56.100
Then lenpa (LEN PA) is like advanced negative coffee meditation.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:04.900
"I don't believe there's any connection between yelling at my kids and my husband yelling at me."

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.390
So those three are all negative thoughts.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:19.609
duje dang sipa nyi le dang
('DU BYED DANG SRID PA GNYIS LAS DANG)--

00:11:19.609 --> 00:11:22.359
link number two and link number ten,

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.420
those two are karma

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.060
but different stages of karma.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.760
Number two is? (fresh karma) Yeah, like watermelon... (just planted)

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:42.760
Yeah. And #10 is? (ripened karma, seeds are fat and ready)

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:48.040
Yeah good, so translate that while I drink my coffee.

00:11:55.949 --> 00:11:57.746
Then he says a strange thing.

00:11:57.746 --> 00:11:59.268
hlakma dun dukngel
(LHAG MA BDUN SDUG BSNGAL)--

00:11:59.268 --> 00:12:01.279
and the other seven, they are suffering.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.020
And then he quotes Ludrup (KLU SGRUB),

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.000
Arya Nagarjuna.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:17.960
And this happens to be the same text about the essence of dependent origination

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:21.580
that we had before. It's very short. It's like one or two pages.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:36.520
So, let's follow the Tibetan, because there's going to be two interesting points here.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.220
dangpo gyepa gu nyonmong
(DANG PO BRGYAD PA DGU NYON MONGS)--

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.660
"the first one, the eighth one, and the nine

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:49.720
are negative thoughts."

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:53.359
The first one, the eighth, and nine.

00:12:54.329 --> 00:12:55.890
You see

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.890
he doesn't say "ninth."

00:12:58.019 --> 00:13:00.739
He says "the nine," Nagarjuna.

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:11.360
Why didn't he say ninth and he just said nine?

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:18.740
Because it's poetry and he didn't have room to put "TH."

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.500
So don't get confused.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.949
You should hear pa (PA)--gupa (DGU PA).

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:39.889
Okay, so now it's clear: number one, number eight, and number nine, these three are negative emotions.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.520
nyipa chupa le yin te
(GNYIS PA BCU PA LAS YIN TE)--

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:49.430
"number two and number ten, (these) are the (two) karmas." These two are karmas.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.640
hlakma dun ni
(LHAG MA BDUN NI)--

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:59.040
now the rest of the seven--"the remaining seven"--

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.810
dukngel yin (SDUG BSNGAL YIN)--these "are suffering."

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.639
Now I always like to go to the original text

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.849
any time, this is a Mixed Nuts rule.

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:21.230
Any time there's a quotation in a book,

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.810
the rule of our Mixed Nuts translation team ...

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.250
we are all

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:36.080
reincarnations of the students of Master Xuanzang in the

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:41.120
Wild Goose Pagoda Tower during the Tangchao.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:48.560
We have a rule:

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:53.820
if there's a quotation, go check it and make sure it's correct.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:03.999
So I checked it, and then I said to myself it's correct.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.589
Then I saw there's one word different.

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:13.720
The way it's quoted in the lam rim,

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.340
The last line says hlakma dun ni (LHAG MA BDUN NI)--

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.700
means now the last, remaining seven,

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.640
they are suffering.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:34.660
But that's a little uncomfortable, right? I mean the others must be suffering also--the whole wheel is suffering.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:47.259
The real ancient Tengyur (BSTAN 'GYUR) version of this verse,

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.180
it says hlakma dun yang (LHAG MA BDUN YANG),

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.600
not ni (NI).

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:00.820
Okay here, look here--hlakma dun ni,

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.400
and this says lhakma dun yang,

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:06.040
which means,

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.399
the remaining seven are "also" pain.

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:17.949
So I think anyone who listened to this class so far,

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:28.089
I can accept that three of those are negative emotions: number one, number eight, and number nine.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.839
I can understand that two of them are karma: number two and number ten.

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:45.040
But why does he say and the remaining seven are suffering?

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:50.860
Why does he say that, because aren't those first five suffering also?

00:16:54.779 --> 00:16:57.648
And if you thought that when you heard me say it first,

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:01.980
you're correct.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:09.080
Because the real verse says, "the remaining seven are also suffering."

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:20.740
So I made some ... my very third-grade childlike drawings here.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:33.889
I put some color around the first, eighth, and ninth links, which are negative emotions.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.900
Then in the next image,

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.860
I put some color around two and ten together.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:55.420
And then in the next image, I put colors around three to seven, and eleven to twelve--these seven.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:08.720
And of course by now, you know that these two groups are kind of the same thing.

00:18:14.789 --> 00:18:16.789
Three, four, five, six, seven,

00:18:18.179 --> 00:18:20.179
and 11 and 12,

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:22.760
they're almost the same thing.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:24.179
Why?

00:18:24.179 --> 00:18:26.298
Three: my mind comes into my mom.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.770
Link four: my body and mind are inside my mom.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:40.640
Link five: my eyes, and ears, and nose, etc., grow inside my mom.

00:18:46.529 --> 00:18:48.979
Link six: they make contact with the outside world.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:57.740
Link seven: because of that contact, I get feelings--like good feelings or bad feelings.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.300
three, four, five, six, seven--

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.380
but they're the same as eleven and twelve.

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:13.280
Eleven and twelve together are one whole human life.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:21.760
I'm born, I get old, and I die.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.260
diy tsik kang dangpo
('DI'I TSIG RKANG DANG PO)--

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:30.060
so those are the three images I put up for you.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.020
diy tsik kang dangpoy de sum kun long dang
('DI'I TSIG RKANG DANG PO'I DE GSUM KUN SLONG DANG)

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.000
He said--interesting--

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:45.900
you can think of the first line--of the verse, okay,

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:56.100
where Nagarjuna says the first, and the eighth, and the ninth, these are the negative emotions--

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:06.260
you can think of those as being the process of motivation to do something bad.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:16.860
Then you can think of the next line--

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:21.200
the next line says number two and number ten are karma--

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.560
If you think about it,

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.479
number two and number ten,

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:35.389
these are karma expressed by doing things or saying things.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.660
Where's the mental karma?

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:49.900
He already covered it, in the first group.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:56.260
The first group, those three mental afflictions are mental karma.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.780
Which means link number one is link number two.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.180
Number two, he says here,

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:20.359
must refer to the things you say and the things you do because of your bad motivation.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:34.220
Why in number two--the potter--did he leave out karma of thinking?

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:45.859
Because that was already in the misunderstanding.

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:50.060
That's karma of the mind.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.820
Okay.

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:55.920
tsik kang sumpay de nam longchu yin
(TSIG RKANG GSUM PA'I DE RNAMS LONGS SPYOD YIN)--

00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:02.000
then in the third line here--which says the other seven are suffering--

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:11.600
these links are just kind of what are the objects in your life that you experience.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:21.880
tendrel chu nyi luk jung dok tu sampay
(RTEN 'BREL BCU GNYIS LUGS 'BYUNG LDOG TU BSAMS PA'I)--

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:24.260
if you contemplate

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:26.840
on these twelve links,

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:31.120
how they happen in order and how you shut them down.

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:39.322
korwa chiy dukngel gompe
('KHOR BA SPYI'I SDUG BSNGAL BSGOMS PAS)--

00:22:39.322 --> 00:22:44.200
then really, you are automatically doing a meditation on the pain of life.

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:57.519
And then automatically there will be a shift in your heart.

00:23:00.470 --> 00:23:05.260
You will start to understand, "Oh my god, I'm like a prisoner in this wheel.

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.200
This world is a prison.

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.220
My life is a prison.

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:19.680
My whole life I've been inside a prison.

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:26.400
And I'm condemned in this prison.

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:30.620
The only way I'd leave this prison is to die."

00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:36.310
And it's not a metaphor; it's real.

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:40.870
No matter how wealthy you are,

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:44.020
no matter how young you are

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:47.680
it doesn't matter--

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.940
you are still locked in the jail of death.

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:05.500
Then, A... number one, you'd be crazy to think that all the people before you died, but you're not going to die.

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:18.669
Then if someone told you, you know, there's a pretty easy way to stop that problem,

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:29.620
then I think you'd have to be crazy not to at least listen to them.

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:38.340
So just the idea, "my life is like a prison

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:42.000
no matter what happens in my life, good or bad,

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:45.560
I will lose everything, even my life."

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:56.740
then finally you get this idea, "Oh, maybe there's a way I can get out.

00:24:57.140 --> 00:24:59.140
I mean, I don't want to die,

00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:03.060
but I would like to change life and make it like a paradise.

00:25:11.820 --> 00:25:14.700
I would like to do that."

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:17.760
Then he says ngejung yin (NGES 'BYUNG YIN)--

00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:21.400
"that's renunciation."

00:25:24.380 --> 00:25:30.260
In English, the word renunciation ... first of all, waiters in restaurants never used this word.

00:25:37.039 --> 00:25:41.739
Even in the ancient Christian tradition where the word came from,

00:25:48.019 --> 00:25:53.529
it means "I will stay in the monastery, I will eat simple food, I will have a simple bed," like that.

00:26:01.340 --> 00:26:05.319
But the word in Buddhism, the original word ngejung,

00:26:11.410 --> 00:26:14.640
it has a different feeling and a different meaning.

00:26:16.740 --> 00:26:22.060
Of course, all of you who studied ACI courses, you know, this is the first of the three principal paths,

00:26:30.740 --> 00:26:34.240
and it's very simple to explain it.

00:26:34.380 --> 00:26:36.580
It just means, "I want to get out!"

00:26:40.300 --> 00:26:45.220
It doesn't mean what it means in the Christian word renunciation; it doesn't mean that.

00:26:51.100 --> 00:26:57.209
It doesn't mean "I will avoid fancy food" or "I won't go on vacations" or "I won't watch movies."

00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:08.519
Buddhism ngejung means "I definitely want to get out of here."

00:27:14.020 --> 00:27:16.320
So your life, from the time you're born ...

00:27:16.420 --> 00:27:19.580
from the minute you are born to the minute you die,

00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:26.000
the whole thing is exactly the same as a prison.

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.380
When you say "This guy is rich," you just mean "This guy has more money in his prison cell,

00:27:35.900 --> 00:27:37.900
that's the same cell that I'm in."

00:27:46.980 --> 00:27:49.140
Or "tTis movie star is very beautiful

00:27:50.890 --> 00:27:57.449
but it just means she's in the same prison cell that I'm in and she's going to lose all her beauty also."

00:28:09.460 --> 00:28:15.090
I don't see this word renunciation meaning "grumpy ordained person."

00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:29.600
In many religious traditions, including Buddhism,

00:28:32.600 --> 00:28:34.780
renunciation,

00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:37.320
the picture in your mind,

00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:41.480
